{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact BR13 head 2284b47343c785a823dc1d931e9ddb6d9fc02cab on builder/version-questions-br13-20261109, tree 86f3511a, all 104 artifacts, for request 487496f5 under promise 4b0e1a79 and review request 5accff08. Code outside `packages/platform` now asks named version questions and relations instead of holding its own pin lists. A golden table of every pin against each old predicate passes unchanged, and no list is unified. The head follows rulings a5522106, 12c4f5fb, 74e0de0d and a2e43e02.\n\nWhat I checked in the source:\n\n- The owners. `packages/platform/src/version-questions.ts` holds 89 questions and `packages/contract/src/catalog-vocabulary.ts` holds 16, each as an exact list of pins. `answersVersionQuestion` dispatches the 16 to the Contract leaf and answers the rest from its own table. Both answer false for any value that is not a listed string, so an unknown or future pin gains no answer from its version number. `version-relations.ts` keeps each consumer's rows, tuple order and empty default, and its record lookups use `Object.hasOwn`.\n- The golden table. `version-questions.test.ts` checks that the question names equal the fixture's 104 predicates plus the standing question, that the catalog pins equal the fixture's 100, and every answer for 105 rows. It also checks the three wrappers in `versions.ts` and the Contract leaf, six non-string inputs, and three named disagreements. The name comparison would fail on a duplicate question across the two tables.\n- The old lists. The fixture and the new table arrive in the same commit, so I compared 12 questions with the predicates they replace on main 19ddc868. These are `cliManifestListDestination`, `viewsEvidenceMembership` and its directory relation, the three Replay questions, six MCP questions and the two authority questions. Where an old predicate compared against a cohort constant, I resolved the constant on main. All 12 lists match exactly.\n- The layering. Contract gains one import-free module and one export. Derive, Git, portable Replay and the seven lower Client readers import that leaf directly, and none imports Platform. Platform re-exports it. The release plan and guide name `./catalog-vocabulary`, and C's `./diff` exclusion survives the merge.\n- The seals. On my own extracted copy of the head, outside the builder's worktree, `scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs` and `scripts/active-source.test.mjs` pass all 24 cases. That run recomputes every changed seal, including authority.ts and the three new owners. The one added architecture path is the fixture exception that ruling 74e0de0d allows.\n- The correspondence. `coverage.json` advances only Editor and Effects to c9f4dff6. The two recorded file hashes equal `retained-editor-data.ts` and `operations.ts` at the head, and both files are unchanged since c9f4dff6.\n- The aliases. Counter's and Lending's Vitest configs and Counter's browser config map `catalog-vocabulary` first, then an anchored bare Contract alias. That fixes gate v4's `ENOTDIR`.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- Scope. Main 19ddc868 is an ancestor, the head is pushed, and the builder's worktree is clean at the head. Against main, the head changes exactly the 104 paths that its 104 artifacts cover. The commit-message check passes: 27 checked, 0 flagged.\n- The gate. I read gate.exit at ff0eee7d, tree f17cb150: \"exit 0\". The launcher, driver and analyzer exits read 0 too. The log records Node, Counting, Plain and Native passed, and the reconciliation records 5,842 passes and three expected skips, with all six Scale cases. Gates v2, v3, v4 and v5b stay recorded as failed. Only the note and four evidence manifests change between ff0eee7d and the head.\n- The browser. GitHub reports Page run 42761381020 attempt 1 as successful, 12 of 12 steps, and Card run 42761385370 attempt 3 as successful, 13 of 13 steps, both at a591595e. Card attempts 1 and 2 stay cancelled. Only the note and six evidence manifests change between a591595e and the head.\n- The evidence. The 18 manifests hash to the values the note cites. Their 1,817 files match their sizes and digests and are read-only. The credential pattern matches four Node compile-cache files, and in each the match is the `-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\\nXXXX` placeholder in a tool's help text. No credential appears.\n\nArchitecture: sound. Each version question now has one named owner, and a consumer states which question it asks. The import-free leaf in Contract keeps every layer below Platform free of a Platform import. One consequence: a question that read a cohort constant now holds a frozen copy of that pin. A later edit to a cohort constant no longer moves the answer, and the golden table catches the change.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The change moves pin lists and adds no grant, route or setting. Each authority-relevant answer, including own standing, session birth, invitation proof and unpublished branches, keeps its exact positive set. Non-string and unknown inputs answer false.\n\nSimplification: no required change. Two notes:\n\n- Several questions hold equal sets, for example `scopeOwnStandingMembership` and `scopeSessionMembership`, `mcpDeviceInstallOptionsRules` and `mcpOwnerFieldRules`, and the two Replay legacy-publication questions. The request keeps them apart on purpose. Merging any pair is a later, separate decision.\n- The note runs to 630 lines, and most of it records checkpoint history. A reader looking for the current state can start at its last two sections.\n\nThe Page asset and Worker sources change. The planner decides the deployment. No setting changes. This approval authorizes no deployment, publication or live acceptance.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d834e241d31c895c1c6aa77cc7e61268f957f796","binding":"assigned","head":"2284b47343c785a823dc1d931e9ddb6d9fc02cab","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1225ccc77ff6d51ee54ed8eff